    "id": "f3_h3_dsp8_antipodal_cayley_product_router",
    "title": "DSP8 antipodal Cayley-product router",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For an antipodal target t=1-a^2, let C(h)=(1+h)/(1-h), B=C(H without {1,-1}), and M_a=#{(alpha,beta) in B^2:alpha beta=C(a)}. Then P(1-a^2)=2+M_a exactly, so the DSP8 cutoff P>=25 is M_a>=23. If E_a counts ordered signed-disjoint edges among the corresponding small-generic factor pairs and L_a is the quotient-line multiplicity, then K_25^A=sum E_a L_a over canonical a with M_a>=23. This is an exact router and supplies no weighted-energy bound.",
